  "findings": [
    "Two different small models execute the chain, but task success is 2/24, equal to direct 2/24; single-node RAG is 1/24. No quality improvement established.",
    "RAG cumulative measured service is about 17-18 times direct under these prompts; quality too low for a reliable task-quality objective.",
    "RAG answers lack FINAL for 5/24 in both modes; 256-token budget reached in 5 single-node and 6 multi-model answers. Query fallback 1/24 vs 4/24; unknown answers 13 vs 11.",
    "Strict match rejects predicted 74 vs gold 74 years, and predicted 103 years vs gold 103. Diagnostic examples do not alter scoring; unknowns and genuinely wrong numbers also fail.",
    "Network-aware policy never improves mean latency in six scenarios. It matches fixed at low rate; at higher rates saves 2.1-4.3 percent bytes with up to 24.6 percent worse mean latency.",
    "Occasional answer placement on shared edge consumes slots needed by subsequent query/retrieval stages. Stage-local greedy predictions can worsen full-chain queues.",
    "Cloud offload can reduce queueing versus same-node RAG under synthetic resources; this does not establish model-cooperation or network-aware quality benefits."
  ],
  "thesis_mapping": {
    "system_model": "Dependent stages, fixed links/nodes, allowed models, FCFS capacity, measured service, application payload/propagation.",
    "optimization_goal": "Task success vs mean/P95 completion latency vs cross-node bytes; implemented greedy estimated stage completion under availability/capacity.",
    "experiment_role": "Feasibility/negative-result pilot, with measured stages and historical queue/network replay explicitly separated.",
    "recommendation": "Keep RAG exploratory; insufficient evidence to designate it the main thesis scenario. Establish reliable retrieval/answer scoring on a fixed expanded sample, then evaluate whole-chain scheduling with measured node calibration."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "Small-sample pilot is not a full FRAMES or MLPerf result",
    "Exact match penalizes valid paraphrases and alternate units",
    "BM25/RRF/lexical reranking replaces dense/ColBERT retrieval",
    "One retrieval round; no iterative sufficiency checking",
    "Network and heterogeneous node speed/capacity are replay assumptions",
    "Model load, ingestion/index construction and orchestration overhead outside task latency",
    "Short warmup does not guarantee all JIT kernels are compiled; residual compilation can inflate early measured requests",
    "Fixed generation budget; budget reached is a token-count diagnostic, not a recorded vLLM finish reason",
    "24 independent questions only; repeated 96-request replay is not added quality evidence.",
    "No link contention, packet loss, background traffic or model residency/switch cost. Edge slot is a synthetic shared model/retrieval compute resource.",
    "In-sample means, no held-out latency predictor or online calibration.",
    "One run per question; model outputs/latencies need not be bitwise reproducible across hardware/kernel versions.",
    "Direct and evidence prompts differ; this pilot does not isolate every cause of latency differences."
  ],
  "validation": {
    "pytest": "138 passed in 2.02s",
    "new_rag_tests": 13,
    "coverage": [
      "fixed sampling",
      "multi-model stage dependencies and failure retention",
      "output budget diagnostics",
      "event order/FCFS/capacity",
      "UTF-8 exact bytes/network formula",
      "latency decomposition/P95",
      "network-sensitive placement",
      "deterministic comparisons",
      "CLI"
    ],
    "data_audit": "2304 rows satisfy latency and byte sums, aligned arrivals and identical multi-model answers.",
    "retrieval_reproduction": "48 saved evidence sets reproduced exactly after deterministic term iteration.",
    "replay_reproduction": "Independent replay CLI reproduces per-request file SHA256 exactly."
  },
  "run_commands": [
    "source /root/miniconda3/etc/profile.d/conda.sh && conda activate scaleflow",
    "python -m scaleflow prepare-rag --config configs/qwen35_frames_rag.yaml --manifest results/phase13_frames_manifest.json",
    "python -m scaleflow run-rag --config configs/qwen35_frames_rag.yaml --manifest results/phase13_frames_manifest.json --output results/phase13_rag_measurements.jsonl --summary results/phase13_rag_measurements_summary.json",
    "python -m scaleflow replay-rag-network --config configs/qwen35_frames_rag.yaml --inputs results/phase13_rag_measurements.jsonl --output results/phase13_rag_network_replay.jsonl --summary results/phase13_rag_network_summary.json",
    "pytest -q"
  ],
